+# T-104 — Deploy plumbing: Dockerfile volume path, fly env, smoke script
+
+Delivered and committed: `3218a68` (`build(deploy): entrypoint volume fix, fly env, smoke script (T-104)`), all five owned paths, this retry after the first attempt was review-BLOCKed for delivering only a handoff.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **`Dockerfile`** (modified, runtime stage only; build stage byte-identical):
+  `su-exec` added to the apk line; `COPY scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh` +
+  `RUN chmod 0755`; `USER appuser` → `USER root` (the entrypoint must chown
+  the root-owned `/data` mount); `ENTRYPOINT ["/docker-entrypoint.sh"]` +
+  `CMD ["/app/server"]`. Alpine stays pinned at 3.22; size impact ≈ 30 KB
+  (su-exec), well under the 40 MB target.
+- **`scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh`** (new, committed mode 100755): POSIX sh,
+  `set -eu`; best-effort `chown -R 10001:10001 /data || true` when `/data`
+  exists (covers local `docker run` without a mount), then
+  `exec su-exec appuser "$@"` so the server stays PID 1 with its signal
+  handling for graceful shutdown.
+- **`fly.toml`** (modified): `[env]` block after `[build]` with exactly
+  `PORT="8080"`, `APP_ENV="prod"`, `DB_PATH="/data/lights.db"`,
+  `PHOTO_DIR="/data/photos"`, `TZ="America/New_York"`,
+  `TOWN_BBOX="42.70,-71.09,42.82,-70.96"`,
+  `BASE_URL="https://groveland-lights.fly.dev"` (comment notes H5 updates it).
+  Names verified against `internal/config/config.go` (`PORT`, `BASE_URL`,
+  `DB_PATH`, `PHOTO_DIR` required; `APP_ENV` accepts `prod`; `TOWN_BBOX`
+  parses via `ParseBBox` with min<max on both axes). Secrets
+  (SESSION_KEY/IP_HASH_KEY/ADMIN_TOKEN) are NOT here — `fly secrets set`
+  only. Snapshot retention stays a volume-creation flag (H4), never a key.
+  Nothing else in the file changed.
+- **`.dockerignore`** (modified): adds `test-run.db`, `test-run-photos/`,
+  `selftest*`; `harness/runs` broadened to `harness`. All 13 prior entries
+  preserved; `scripts/` stays in the build context (the entrypoint is COPYed).
+- **`scripts/smoke.sh`** (new, committed mode 100755): the deployed evidence
+  collector, written against the frozen T-103 probe contract
+  (`harness/tasks/T-103.md`; `#probe-count` span, hidden `csrf_token` input,
+  valid HTMX POST → 200, no-JS → 303, tampered → 403 with unchanged count,
+  `/healthz` → 200 `ok`, CSP on every response per
+  `internal/web/web.go withSecurityHeaders`). Steps print
+  `smoke: <check> OK` and the header carries UTC date + git sha so two runs
+  around a deploy prove counter persistence. bash 3.2-safe: no associative
+  arrays, no `${var,,}`, no mapfile; `set -euo pipefail`.
+
+## Reviewer advisories folded in (both reviews of the first attempt)
+
+1. **macOS `%Z` date parse removed entirely**: TLS expiry now uses
+   `openssl x509 -checkend 1209600` (14 d) — no BSD/GNU date parsing at all.
+   The cert is fetched once (`s_client | openssl x509 > cert.pem`) and read
+   twice (`-enddate` for the printed evidence, `-checkend` for the assertion).
+2. **No silent `set -e` aborts**: every curl invocation (healthz, index,
+   probe GETs via `probe_get`, both POSTs) carries `|| die "..."`, so every
+   failure path prints `smoke: FAIL: <reason>`. Extraction helpers return
+   non-zero on no-match and their callers `|| die`.
+3. **`N₁ = N₀ + 1` race**: documented as a single-admin deployment
+   assumption with an explicit re-run-before-escalating comment in the script.
+4. **Argument hygiene**: a second positional or unknown flag errors out with
+   `usage` instead of silently overwriting `BASE_URL`; `--help` exits 0.
+5. **csrf extraction**: matches `<input[^>]*name="csrf_token"[^>]*>` —
+   order-independent — then pulls `value="..."`; comment pins the T-102
+   unpadded-base64url assumption (no `"` inside tokens).
+6. **CSP grep is case-sensitive** (`^Content-Security-Policy:`), correct
+   because Go canonicalizes header names on send.
+7. **Exec bits are in the commit** (`git diff --cached --summary` shows
+   `create mode 100755` for both scripts) — staged via
+   `git add --chmod=+x` because `chmod` is permission-denied in this sandbox.
+8. **200/303**: the packet's step 4 says accept either, so both are accepted,
+   but the observed status is printed in the OK line and a comment cites the
+   frozen contract (HTMX-flagged POST should be 200; 303 is the no-JS
+   fallback), so a regression would be visible in the output.
+
+## How verified (this session, with exit codes)
+
+| Command | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `make check-fast` | exit 0 — fmt-check, `go vet`, `golangci-lint: 0 issues.`, `-race` unit tests ok (`cmd/harness`, `internal/config`, `internal/web`) |
+| `make e2e-task TASK=T-104` | exit 0, prints `no claims for T-104` (expected: `claims: []` — nothing to run) |
+| `git add --chmod=+x …` + `git diff --cached --summary` | `create mode 100755` for both scripts |
+| `git diff --cached --check` | empty (no whitespace errors) |
+| `git commit -m …` | exit 0 → `3218a68`; lefthook pre-commit gitleaks: `no leaks found`; commit-msg conventional check passed |
+| Read-back of all five files | byte-exact against the intended content (two-pass write: first pass mangled `\n` literals via zsh echo escapes, caught by read-back and fixed) |
+| `make doctor` | exit 2 — PRE-EXISTING: `flyctl` version parse (`WANT 0.5.8 GOT 2026-11-11T17:19:17Z`); not introduced by this task, doctor is not in check-fast/ci |
+
+Unit tests: none added — the packet owns no test path, claims no assertion,
+and its hard constraint caps machine verification at `make check-fast` +
+reading + hygiene. The shell logic is exercised by the deployed smoke run
+itself (the packet's stated judge path).
+
+## Machine-unverified paths (for human / CI)
+
+This session denied docker, flyctl, curl, shellcheck and even `bash -n`
+(detail below), so none of the following ran here:
+
+1. **Static shell checks**: `bash -n scripts/smoke.sh
+   scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh` and `shellcheck scripts/smoke.sh
+   scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh` (shellcheck 0.11.0 is installed and pinned
+   in `make doctor`; no Makefile target wraps it, and direct invocation is
+   permission-denied here).
+2. **Image build + size** (CI runs this via `make ci` → `docker-build`):
+   `docker build -t groveland-lights:dev .` — expect ~29.3 MB.
+3. **Entrypoint + volume path**:
+   `docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 -v gl-data:/data -e PORT=8080
+   -e APP_ENV=prod -e BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
+   -e TOWN_BBOX='42.70,-71.09,42.82,-70.96'
+   -e SESSION_KEY=<32+ bytes> -e IP_HASH_KEY=<32+ bytes>
+   -e ADMIN_TOKEN=<32+ bytes> groveland-lights:dev`
+   then `docker exec` in and confirm `/data/lights.db` exists owned by
+   `10001:10001`. Without a volume mount the server must still boot
+   (chown `|| true`; DB_PATH must then point somewhere writable).
+4. **Fly deploy**: `flyctl deploy --ha=false` (config is parsed/validated as
+   part of deploy). Before first deploy: `flyctl secrets set SESSION_KEY=…
+   IP_HASH_KEY=… ADMIN_TOKEN=…` and `flyctl volumes create data --region ewr
+   --snapshot-retention 14` (H4). Note: `config.Load` does NOT hard-require
+   the three secrets (they are read via `secret()` which tolerates absence),
+   so a deploy that forgets them boots with nil keys — the runbook must treat
+   `fly secrets set` as mandatory before first deploy.
+5. **Deployed smoke evidence** (needs T-103 merged and deployed):
+   `scripts/smoke.sh https://groveland-lights.fly.dev` before and after a
+   redeploy — the second run's `smoke: probe count N0 -> N1` line continuing
+   from the first run's N1 is the M1 persistence evidence. Full suite:
+   `scripts/smoke.sh https://groveland-lights.fly.dev --smoke-suite`
+   (runs `make smoke BASE_URL=…`; note that target uses
+   `--pass-with-no-tests`, so until @smoke specs are activated by T-105 a
+   suite pass alone proves nothing — the curl-level probe assertions above
+   are the real check).
+
+## Open issues
+
+1. **Sandbox write path (environment, disclosed)**: this session, like the
+   first attempt, denied the `write`/`edit` tools on owned paths and almost
